WHEN DO YOU NEED A COMMERCIAL LICENSE?

You need a commercial license if you want to:
- Distribute Linky or derivative works in a proprietary product
- Use Linky without making your modifications open source
- Remove or modify attribution requirements
- Sell Linky or incorporate it into a paid product
- Use Linky in a business without complying with GPLv3

You DON'T need a commercial license if you:
- Use Linky for personal, educational, or non-profit projects
- Contribute back your modifications as open source under GPLv3
- Deploy Linky in an internal tool without distributing it externally
